<article class="env-lemma" id="0AWD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AWD">Lemma <span data-tag="0AWD">47.22.1</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a local homomorphism of Noetherian local rings. Let $\omega _ A^\bullet $ be a normalized dualizing complex. If $A \to B$ is flat and $\mathfrak m_ A B = \mathfrak m_ B$, then $\omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A B$ is a normalized dualizing complex for $B$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It is clear that $\omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A B$ is in $D^ b_{\textit{Coh}}(B)$. Let $\kappa _ A$ and $\kappa _ B$ be the residue fields of $A$ and $B$. By More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0A6A" data-tag="0A6A">15.101.2</a> we see that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ B(\kappa _ B, \omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A B) = R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(\kappa _ A, \omega _ A^\bullet ) \otimes _ A B = \kappa _ A[0] \otimes _ A B = \kappa _ B[0]  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Thus $\omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A B$ has finite injective dimension by More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0AVJ" data-tag="0AVJ">15.71.7</a>. Finally, we can use the same arguments to see that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ B(\omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A B, \omega _ A^\bullet \otimes _ A B) = R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(\omega _ A^\bullet , \omega _ A^\bullet ) \otimes _ A B = A \otimes _ A B = B  \]
</div>
    <p>
       as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>